  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
  Elisp functions and keybinds for running a Forester server, starting, stopping, etc. Have a log/status buffer. Start the server whenever a Forester file is opened and keep it running
</html:p>
    <html:p><html:code>SPC r B</html:code> does correctly open the browser, but currently does so at the wrong path. For instance, this tree opens <html:code>file:///sss-003C/index.xml</html:code>. But to actually see it in a browser, we should open the route <html:code>http://localhost:1313/sss-003C/index.xml</html:code> (or at whatever port the current server is on).
</html:p>
    <html:p>
  We could then show in the editor if there is a build error for the tree. Is related to what language servers should do?
</html:p>
